  "format_notes": "Each chart maps a tournament size (the number of first-round slots) to the ordered list of slot positions that receive BYEs when teams are short. The Nth BYE awarded goes to position byes[N-1] in the chart. Apply byes in order until the team-count gap is filled. Reading the source string: '1 @32 2 @16 3 @24 ...' means the 1st BYE goes to slot 32, 2nd to slot 16, 3rd to slot 24, etc. The trailing '**' in the original APA text marks end-of-list.",
  "usage_example": "For a 32-slot chart with 24 teams playing, 8 BYEs are needed. Take the first 8 entries of charts['32'] => [32, 16, 24, 8, 28, 12, 20, 4]. Those slots receive BYEs; the remaining 24 slots hold teams.",
  "modified_chart_notes": "Sizes 12, 24, 48, 96 are 'modified' charts that aren't pure powers of two. Their BYE placement reuses the chart of the next-smaller equivalent: 12 reuses 4, 24 reuses 8, 48 reuses 16, 96 reuses 32. The list length therefore reflects the underlying base chart, not the modified slot count.",

